{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789465828,"nonce":"t+nmxBNqRdwxlAC31ArP7enML60=","title":"A headroom gate before an LLVM promotion, with refusals memoised","message":"Promotion to the LLVM tier is decided by invocation counts and OSR requests; nothing asks whether LLVM can improve on the Cranelift code. A function with no loop and nothing but a call has no headroom at any tier, and its promotion costs a compile, the backend lock, and (until 107df3c) its whole callee closure. Ash gates on `llvm_ceiling` (a function's ceiling read off its IR: loops, arithmetic density, calls that could inline) and remembers every refusal, since the broker re-proposes the same function tens of thousands of times (`gate_rejected`, `tier0_refused` in ash_interp/src/tiering.rs).\n\nAdd the same in `install_promotion_requester`/the promotion path: a per-function ceiling from the HIR (loop headers, instruction mix, whether the OSR layout is accepted), a refusal memo, and `ZYNTAX_PROMOTE_GATE=0` to disable it for measurement. Report gate decisions under ZYNTAX_TRACE_TIER_UP.","files":null}]}